  "method": "Centre line of the oval CEBAF tunnel, derived from located buildings of the City of Newport News footprint layer, whose building numbers are the lab's own (the list on JLab's site plan, src:geo-jlab-site-plan-detail). (1) Straights: the footprints 'Jefferson Lab #999-01' and '#999-02' ('999 Accelerator Tunnel', labelled twice on the site plan) are two parallel strips 265 m long and 4.5-5 m wide (the tunnel is 'about 14 feet across and 10 feet high'); their axes point 26.4 degrees north of east (bearing 63.6 degrees) and are 160.7 m apart. The straights are drawn along those two axes and extended to the arc tangent points; the North Extractor Service (#21), South Extractor Service (#82) and Injector Service (#53) buildings lie within 1.5 m of the extended lines. (2) Arcs: the eight arc service buildings of the site plan (East Arc Service E2-E5 = #39, #49, #63, #50; West Arc Service W2-W5 = #68, #56, #40, #45) lie on two semicircles. Fitting each semicircle to its three apex buildings (E3-E5, W3-W5) with its centre on the mid-line between the straights gives a radius of 80.3 m, equal to half the straight separation (80.3 m) to within 0.1 m, residuals 0.2-0.6 m (E2 0.2 m, W2 4.4 m); the arcs are therefore drawn as semicircles tangent to both straights, centres 403.4 m apart along the axis. (3) Length: this centre line is 1311 m; the official pages say 'The oval-shaped tunnel is about 7/8 of a mile long' (1408 m): -6.9%, inside the half-step of an eighth-of-a-mile rounding (13/16 to 15/16 mile = 1310 to 1508 m) but not a confirmation of the shape. What is not in the data: the straight lengths beyond the two 265 m strips are inferred from the arc tangent points, and the beam switchyard and hall access tunnels are not drawn. Straights are as located as the city footprints (a few metres); the arcs rest on service buildings that sit on, not necessarily exactly over, the tunnel, so accuracy_m is 20. Haversine on R = 6371008.8 m.",
  "name": "CEBAF racetrack tunnel centre line (derived from located footprints and arc service buildings)",
  "notes": [
    "Official-versus-derived length: 1311 m derived against 'about 7/8 of a mile' (1408 m) is a -6.9% conflict that the rounding of the official figure can absorb; it is listed in the worklog as a source conflict."
  ],
